Subject: [PATCH] fpcmoh: drain the a921's twelfth capture record

The a921 sends one more record per capture than the eleven fixed read
states consume. That record carries the last 24 bytes of the image
message (the message is 11288 = 11 * 1024 + 24), so without draining it
the enclave is handed 11264 bytes, fpc_enclave_process_data() returns -6
on every record, and the stray record is then eaten by the dead-pixel
read, which desynchronises the TLS stream (`ssl error 1`).

Enable the same read-remaining drain the a900 uses. FP_ENROLL_X_POSTDRAIN
then reads the trailing record, feeds it to the TLS ring and calls
fpc_enclave_process_data(), completing the message.

---
 libfprint/drivers/fpcmoh/fpc.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/fpcmoh/fpc.c b/libfprint/drivers/fpcmoh/fpc.c
--- a/libfprint/drivers/fpcmoh/fpc.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/fpcmoh/fpc.c
@@ -2206,8 +2206,14 @@
     {
     case 0x9800:
-    case 0xA921:
       self->max_enroll_stage = MAX_ENROLL_SAMPLES;
       break;
 
+    case 0xA921:
+      self->max_enroll_stage = MAX_ENROLL_SAMPLES;
+      /* patches/0017: one more record per capture than the eleven fixed
+       * read states consume; it carries the last 24 bytes of the image. */
+      self->read_remaining = TRUE;
+      break;
+
     case 0xA900:
       /* patches/0010: this sensor's matcher wants sixteen samples. */
       self->max_enroll_stage = MAX_ENROLL_SAMPLES_A900;
